# Python standards

- Python 3.10+, type hints on public functions
- `from __future__ import annotations` at the top of every module
- Module docstring explains **why the module exists**, not what the language does
- Imports: standard library, then third-party, then local
- No bare `except:` — catch what you can handle
- Max line length 100
- No leftover print-debugging

## Module boundaries

See the responsibility table in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. In short:

- `src/data.py` knows nothing about models
- `src/pipeline.py` orchestrates; it does not train
- `src/retrieval.py` ranks; it never modifies the text it returns
- `main.py` wires the CLI; it holds no business logic
- No module writes outside `out/` and `data/`
